0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 531.00 Td (* Standard Unix system calls \(`fork`, `exec`, `wait`, `pipe`, `read`, `write`, `sleep`, etc.\).) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 514.50 Td (* A block cache and hierarchical filesystem with logging for crash recovery.) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 498.00 Td (In its default release, xv6 employs a rudimentary, unweighted **Round-Robin** scheduler that) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 485.50 Td (treats every process identically regardless of its execution characteristics.) Tj ET
0.15 0.30 0.50 rg BT /F2 11 Tf 50.00 458.00 Td (1.6 What Problem Does This Project Solve?) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 439.00 Td (The default xv6 Round-Robin scheduler assigns every process an identical time slice \(1 timer) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 426.50 Td (tick\). While simple, this algorithm suffers from significant operational flaws:) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 410.00 Td (1. **Inefficiency for Compute-Heavy Workloads:** CPU-bound jobs \(e.g., scientific) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 397.50 Td (calculations, image rendering\) spend unnecessary CPU overhead repeatedly switching contexts) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 385.00 Td (every single tick \(saving and restoring registers, flushing TLB entries, invalidating caches\)) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 372.50 Td (rather than executing long, uninterrupted compute bursts.) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 356.00 Td (2. **Poor Interactive Responsiveness:** Interactive jobs \(e.g., terminal shells, command-line) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 343.50 Td (editors\) that spend 99% of their time waiting for user keystrokes and only require tiny) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 331.00 Td (fractions of CPU bursts to respond must wait in the common queue behind compute-bound) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 318.50 Td (processes.) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 302.00 Td (3. **Lack of Priority Awareness:** All processes are treated as identical. There is no) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 289.50 Td (mechanism to favor latency-sensitive processes or demote CPU hogs.) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 273.00 Td (This project implements a complete **Multi-Level Feedback Queue \(MLFQ\)** scheduler in) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 260.50 Td (xv6-riscv. MLFQ dynamically learns process behavior through runtime observation, awards high) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 248.00 Td (priority and short response latency to interactive processes, grants larger compute quanta to) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 235.50 Td (CPU-bound processes, prevents starvation through periodic priority boosting, and exposes kernel) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 223.00 Td (scheduling telemetry to user space through the `getpinfo\(\)` system call.) Tj ET
