0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 731.00 Td (A **Context Switch** is the low-level mechanism that suspends execution of one process and) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 718.50 Td (resumes execution of another. It involves:) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 702.00 Td (1. Saving general-purpose registers \(callee-saved registers: `s0`-`s11`, stack pointer `sp`,) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 689.50 Td (return address `ra`\) of the current thread onto its stack or context struct.) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 673.00 Td (2. Changing the active stack pointer to the target thread's stack.) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 656.50 Td (3. Restoring the saved registers of the new thread.) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 640.00 Td (4. Changing the memory mapping \(switching the `satp` register to point to the new user page) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 627.50 Td (table and flushing the TLB via `sfence.vma`\).) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 611.00 Td (5. Returning to execution in the new process context.) Tj ET
