0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 731.00 Td (> **Every $N$ ticks \(`BOOST_INTERVAL`\), all existing processes in the system are boosted back) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 718.50 Td (to Q0, and their current quantum counters are reset to zero.**) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 702.00 Td (This guarantees:) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 685.50 Td (1. **Starvation Prevention:** No process can ever be starved for more than $N$ ticks. Even a) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 673.00 Td (process at Q3 is guaranteed a run in Q0 every boost cycle.) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 656.50 Td (2. **Dynamic Behavior Adaptation:** If a CPU-bound process becomes interactive, it is) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 644.00 Td (automatically restored to Q0 during the boost and can remain at high priority as long as it) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 631.50 Td (yields before consuming full quanta.) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 615.00 Td (3. **Statistical Integrity:** The cumulative historical tick counters \(`p->ticks[0..3]`\) are) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 602.50 Td (**preserved** across the boost, ensuring accurate accounting and telemetry for `getpinfo\(\)`.) Tj ET
