0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 556.00 Td (1. **Rule 1:** If $\\text{Priority}\(A\) < \\text{Priority}\(B\)$ \(numerically smaller index =) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 543.50 Td (higher priority\), $A$ runs and $B$ does not.) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 527.00 Td (2. **Rule 2:** If $\\text{Priority}\(A\) == \\text{Priority}\(B\)$, $A$ and $B$ run in Round-Robin) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 514.50 Td (fashion using the time slice of that queue.) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 498.00 Td (3. **Rule 3:** When a job enters the system \(`allocproc` / `kfork`\), it is placed at Q0.) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 481.50 Td (4. **Rule 4:** Once a job uses up its time allotment at a given level \(regardless of how many) Tj ET
