0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 438.00 Td (1. Worker A \(PID 4, Heavy CPU\):) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 421.50 Td (* Traversed queues down to Q3 because it burned continuous CPU without yielding.) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 405.00 Td (* Received large 8-tick quanta in Q3, minimizing context-switching overhead.) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 388.50 Td (* When periodic boost occurred at tick 40, was boosted back to Q0!) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 372.00 Td (2. Worker B \(PID 5, Medium Compute\):) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 355.50 Td (* Alternated between computation and yields; demoted through intermediate queues.) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 339.00 Td (3. Worker C \(PID 6, Interactive Yield/IO\):) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 322.50 Td (* Relinquished the CPU via short bursts and pauses; retained top priority \(Q0/Q1\).) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 306.00 Td (* Guarantees immediate response time for interactive user operations!) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 289.50 Td (4. Worker D & Worker E \(PID 7 & 8, I/O-Bound\):) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 273.00 Td (* Slept on timer channels; sleeping ticks were NOT charged to CPU usage.) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 256.50 Td (* Woke up into the highest-priority queue \(Q0\), giving zero-latency I/O response.) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 240.00 Td (=========================================================================================) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 223.50 Td (Notice: Throughout the entire test, PIDs 4, 5, 6, 7, and 8 NEVER changed!) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 207.00 Td (All queue transfers occurred solely within the exact same 5 processes.) Tj ET
